body:
Develop a theory/methods paper only around target-native, falsifiable transfers from quantum information and quantum algorithms into ORION scientific navigation.

Candidate mechanisms:

- quotient/syndrome compression;
- noncommuting operation scheduling;
- resource monotones and conversion witnesses;
- tensor/factor graph contraction;
- adaptive measurement and experiment selection;
- phase-boundary analysis;
- alternative recovery/support families;
- contextuality as a warning against globally sufficient scalar state.

Every bridge must include source theorem, target mapping, correspondence, negative twin, full oracle/compiler/verification resource accounting, and held-out target consequence. Quantum structure does not imply physical quantum validity or quantum advantage. The strongest paper requires multi-domain target-native gains and independent resource review.
